Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Common-terminal current sharing", "Title",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"f2a2cf24-8482-fd4f-a08f-d7d83958b0d6"],

Cell["\:7f2a\:96e8\:8f69 / Miao Yuxuan \[CenterDot] \:6dee\:5357\:5e08\:8303\
\:5b66\:9662 / Huainan Normal University", "Subtitle",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"d8bd6953-62d8-9640-b7dc-c13bac39adc0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Model, inputs and scope", "Section",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"93770275-852e-1040-80dc-9b24a78c7f5c"],

Cell["Zi+e=V1; 1\:1d40i=It", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"9c07fa42-c0b7-1945-889c-b18e9573b86e"],

Cell["SI; exp(+j omega t); RMS; sigma=58 MS/m; mu_r=1; 20 C", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"c4806cfd-c458-f746-a291-20ac9526db54"],

Cell["\<\
Change strand count or return geometry; inspect complex strand currents and \
input/loss balance.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"e7ca961a-d72f-4749-ad57-81c1ba7381a8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Derivation and interpretation", "Section",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"ae8d2862-d929-ed40-a4bb-09d9ebe76aae"],

Cell["\<\
Insulated strands are connected in parallel only at the ends. The 2D Az weak \
form couples each conductive region to its unknown axial electric potential \
gradient. A controlled conducting coaxial return closes the transport problem.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"43cdc231-4c93-7341-b2a5-9d4bd65232a0"],

Cell["\<\
Linearity yields a coupled block system for Az and the source/return voltage \
gradients. Impose \[CapitalSigma]Ii=20 A RMS and Ireturn=\[Minus]20 A; every \
strand shares the source voltage gradient, while each complex Ii follows from \
integrating its solved current density.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"64790043-9497-f74d-8d63-7eaea79082f5"],

Cell["\<\
Compute bundle and return Joule losses separately and compare their sum with \
input real power. Rac,bundle=Pbundle/|It|\.b2 is valid for this pure \
transport case. Seven strands demonstrate the method and do not meet Q2 \
copper area.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"d70b619d-0c2d-8a4b-9235-137dd9acb6e4"],

